      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Saturation magnetization will decrease by less than approximately 10% relative to undoped FeCoNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing can alter or improve saturation magnetization in FeCoNi-based alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis; conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9079992::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Two-phase FeCoNi-based alloys can have greater coercivity than corresponding single-phase fcc or bcc alloys.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9079992::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoFeNi can form an ordered B2 phase, and its phase constitution depends on annealing temperature.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
